
Quantity validation and boundary errors
Severity: High for incorrect order quantities;
  Medium for validation-message issues.
  
Test the quantity field for both Piece and Case purchase modes.
Test input	Expected behavior
Empty quantity	Show required-field validation or use a documented default
0	Reject
1	Accept if stock is available
99	Accept if stock is available
100	Reject if the maximum is 99
-1	Reject
1.5	Reject fractional quantity
abc	Reject nonnumeric input
1.0	Confirm integer-format handling against the requirement
1e2	Reject if scientific notation is unsupported
@#$	Reject invalid characters
  
Very long number	Reject safely without crashing
Leading/trailing spaces	Trim or reject consistently
Blank after editing	Prevent unintended addition
A suitable validation message is: “Quantity must be a whole number from 1 to 99.”
Check that invalid input never adds an item to the cart and never changes the cart total.
